        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=3(x+1)^2-2$. Concave up; vertex $(-1,-2)$; axis $x=-1$; $y$-intercept $(0,1)$; $x$-intercepts $\\left(-1\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac23},0\\right)$.",
          "worked": "The supplied working gives $y=3(x+1)^2-2$. Since $3>0$, the parabola is concave up, with vertex $(-1,-2)$ and axis $x=-1$.\n\nLet $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3(0+1)^2-2\\\\y&=1\\end{aligned}$$\nThe $y$-intercept is $(0,1)$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}3(x+1)^2-2&=0\\\\(x+1)^2&=\\frac23\\\\x+1&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac23}\\\\x&=-1\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac23}\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
