            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$y=2x^2+12x+1$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$y=2(x+3)^2-17$. Concave up; vertex $(-3,-17)$; axis $x=-3$; $y$-intercept $(0,1)$; $x$-intercepts $\\left(-3\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{2}},0\\right)$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2\\left(x^2+6x+\\frac12\\right)\\\\y&=2\\left(x^2+6x+9-9+\\frac12\\right)\\\\y&=2\\left((x+3)^2-\\frac{17}{2}\\right)\\\\y&=2(x+3)^2-17\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $2>0$, the parabola is concave up. The vertex is $(-3,-17)$ and the axis is $x=-3$.\n\nLet $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2(0+3)^2-17\\\\y&=1\\end{aligned}$$\nThe $y$-intercept is $(0,1)$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(x+3)^2-17&=0\\\\(x+3)^2&=\\frac{17}{2}\\\\x+3&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{2}}\\\\x&=-3\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{2}}\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": [
