        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-3\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2+\\frac{35}{4}$. Concave down; vertex $\\left(-\\frac32,\\frac{35}{4}\\right)$; axis $x=-\\frac32$; $y$-intercept $(0,2)$; $x$-intercepts $\\left(-\\frac32\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{105}}6,0\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=-3\\left(x^2+3x-\\frac23\\right)\\\\y&=-3\\left(x^2+3x+\\frac94-\\frac94-\\frac23\\right)\\\\y&=-3\\left(\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2-\\frac{35}{12}\\right)\\\\y&=-3\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2+\\frac{35}{4}\\end{aligned}$$\nSince $-3<0$, the parabola is concave down. The vertex is $\\left(-\\frac32,\\frac{35}{4}\\right)$ and the axis is $x=-\\frac32$.\n\nLet $x=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}y&=-3\\left(0+\\frac32\\right)^2+\\frac{35}{4}\\\\y&=2\\end{aligned}$$\nThe $y$-intercept is $(0,2)$.\n\nLet $y=0$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}-3\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2+\\frac{35}{4}&=0\\\\\\left(x+\\frac32\\right)^2&=\\frac{35}{12}\\\\x+\\frac32&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{35}{12}}\\\\x&=-\\frac32\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{105}}6\\end{aligned}$$",
